From jjj at stowers.org  Fri Jun  6 22:11:58 2014
From: jjj at stowers.org (Johnston, Jeffrey)
Date: Fri, 6 Jun 2014 20:11:58 +0000
Subject: [BioC] Approaches to building Rle sequences from ranges
In-Reply-To: <CANGCfM+E1B-duY7FKGFi-uQmg5sp91JcVG01vfKDCbrmy0dsAw@mail.gmail.com>
References: <CANGCfM+E1B-duY7FKGFi-uQmg5sp91JcVG01vfKDCbrmy0dsAw@mail.gmail.com>
Message-ID: <8E847CC7-6C54-435A-937B-DEB9223C30EA@stowers.org>

For GRanges with a metadata column, you can do:

coverage(granges, weight=?variable?)

This will produce an RleList where the value at each coordinate is the sum of the ?variable? metadata column of all overlapping ranges. I think this will work for your use case if your ranges do not overlap.

-Jeff

On Jun 6, 2014, at 2:59 PM, Vince S. Buffalo <vsbuffalo at ucdavis.edu> wrote:

> Hi All,
> 
