From smyth at wehi.EDU.AU  Mon Jun 16 05:30:59 2014
From: smyth at wehi.EDU.AU (Gordon K Smyth)
Date: Mon, 16 Jun 2014 13:30:59 +1000 (AUS Eastern Standard Time)
Subject: [BioC] edgeR and DESeq2: model design and estimation of
	dispersion
In-Reply-To: <Pine.WNT.4.64.1406141105370.9864@PC975.wehi.edu.au>
References: <8BB3E09A21716943823A352D085EA731DB031B93@ekekmbx00.ekmd.huji.uni>
	<6C1C2EC2-3C69-45C4-AD18-987AE16B363A@ekmd.huji.ac.il>
	<Pine.WNT.4.64.1406141105370.9864@PC975.wehi.edu.au>
Message-ID: <Pine.WNT.4.64.1406161329170.6064@PC975.wehi.edu.au>

Dear Iddo,

No, it is not valid to use a different design matrix for the dispersion 
estimation.

edgeR will handle your model with 400 samples, but it will admitedly be 
slow. If this is too slow, then switch to voom() in the limma package, 
which will be very fast, or to glmQLFTest() in the edgeR package, which 
will still be relatively slow but faster than the glm routines in edgeR 
(or DESeq2).

Best wishes
Gordon


